load @/code/algebra/cayley-dickson
  find cayley-dickson-double

load @/code/algebra/normed-division
  find normed-division-algebra

note <The octonions are the Cayley-Dickson double of the quaternions, the eight-dimensional normed division algebra. They are the last rung of the tower. The input quaternions are associative, so the double keeps the norm, but the octonions are themselves the first non-associative algebra, so doubling once more, to the sedenions, loses the norm. So the octonions are the maximal reversible algebra, the upper jaw of the pinch-point.>

form octonion
  link source, like cayley-dickson-double
  link algebra, like normed-division-algebra
